From a4cdbb237cd7472212c92d655a05567f0c9a21e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:17:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Garden: persistent plants, new plant types, hanging plants,
 scrollable shelf

Plant labels and interaction
- Tapped plants show emoji + name as plain colored text (no pill/border/shadow), centered over
  the plant and kept outside the swaying button. Day/night colors keep 4.5:1 contrast.
- Each plant has its own sway and label timers: several plants can sway at once and tapping one
  never cancels another. Re-tapping a swaying plant restarts its sway.
- Plants are real <button> elements; weather window is keyboard operable; reduced-motion fade.
- Float animation is vertical only; shelf spacing tightened.

Persistent garden
- New saved `garden` record (earned plant ids + highest-ever numbers). Earned plants are never
  removed, each milestone is awarded once, and a streak reset cannot shrink plants or the window vine.
- Plant catalog (data/gardenPlants.ts) + artwork map (components/gardenArt.tsx) make adding plants
  a two-line change. New: Pothos (hanging), Fern, Monstera, Daisy. Next unearned plant grows as a seedling.
- Older saves are backfilled silently from reading history on first load. Backup restore merges
  plants instead of removing them.
- "A new plant has arrived!" card, shown once per newly earned plant.
- Shelf scrolls sideways, hanging plants hang from a rail, very large gardens skip off-screen artwork.

App.tsx: remove the duplicate <MissingCoversButton /> render.
